---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Caffeine Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Caffeine Easy - Know When Your Caffeine Clears iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/caffeine-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed space-y-8">
          <div>
            <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Caffeine Easy?</p>
            <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Caffeine%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <div class="space-y-6">
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does caffeine half-life work?</h3>
                <p>Caffeine has an average half-life of about 5.7 hours. This means that every 5.7 hours, your body metabolizes half of the caffeine in your system. For example, if you drink a 100mg coffee at noon, you'll have about 50mg at 5:42 PM, 25mg at 11:24 PM, and so on until it's effectively cleared.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What does "Clear By" mean?</h3>
                <p>The "Clear by" time is when the caffeine in your system drops under your sleep threshold: 50 mg unless you change it in Settings, where you can pick anything from 25 to 100 mg. It's an estimate to help you plan your last coffee of the day, not medical advice.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is the half-life the same for everyone?</h3>
                <p>The 5.7-hour half-life is an average. Individual metabolism varies based on genetics, liver function, medications, pregnancy, smoking status, and other factors. Your personal half-life could be anywhere from 3 to 7+ hours. The app provides a good general estimate.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How accurate are the preset caffeine amounts?</h3>
                <p>Caffeine content varies widely by preparation method, bean type, and serving size. Our presets use industry-standard averages: ~95mg for an 8oz brewed coffee, ~63mg for espresso, ~47mg for black tea, etc. If you know your drink's caffeine, type it with the drink (for example "Cold brew 180 mg") or change it in the drink's sheet.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Caffeine Easy read my health data?</h3>
                <p>No. Caffeine Easy only <em>writes</em> caffeine intake data (dietaryCaffeine) to HealthKit if you grant permission. It does not read any health data from Apple Health.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why does my caffeine level show high in the morning?</h3>
                <p>If you drank caffeine late in the day, some may still be in your system the next morning. Caffeine takes roughly 5-6 half-lives (~30 hours) to fully clear. A late-night coffee can definitely linger into the next day.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I edit or delete logged entries?</h3>
                <p>Yes. Tap a drink on Today or in History to change its name, caffeine or time, or to delete it. Touch and hold a drink to log it again. Your caffeine level updates right away, and so does Apple Health if you've turned it on.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does the widget update in real-time?</h3>
                <p>The widget works out your level every 15 minutes, and at the moment you're clear, from the drinks you've logged, so it stays current without opening the app.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
